on curcumin curcumin is a molecule found

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.440
inside the turmeric spice and that's

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.640
been extensively researched on its

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.160
benefits some that I've covered in the

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:03.040
past but there's been a ton of work in

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.360
relation to rheumatoid and

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.400
osteoarthritis curcumin Works through a

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.520
number of mechanisms and I'd like to get

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.960
into some of the detail in some of these

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.280
mechanisms in other content because they

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.960
deserve their own deep Dives but for now

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.799
know that curcumin molecule reduces the

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.000
expression or the production of key

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:25.159
inflammation molecules like inter lucans

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.560
interferons tumor necrosis Factor

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:30.640
essentially cumin stops these molecules

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:33.640
from being produced by if we take short

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.880
stroll through your cells binding a

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:39.479
protein complex called inhibitor of

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:43.040
Kappa beta kyes complex will abbreviate

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:45.320
it as ik K curcumin is able to stop

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.680
specific proteins that Branch off this

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.479
complex from binding the genes that

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.200
produce the inflammatory molecules that

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:55.040
we just went over so the inter lucans

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.119
interferons and so on normally if these

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.960
proteins were to peel off and bind these

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:01.719
genes these genes would be red and more

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.360
of these inflammatory molecules would be

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:07.880
produced leading to a stronger immune

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:10.959
response and more pain signals obviously

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:13.360
not what we want in arthritis cumin

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:15.440
attempts to stop that from happening but

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.440
beyond the direct anti-inflammatory

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.080
effects it can also inhibit the

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.160
overactivity of synovial cells in the

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.160
